docs {
  # Group Checklist

  Each group has one checklist. It is available even when empty. Apply `20261120001512_create_checklist_items.sql` with `go run ./cmd/migrate up` before starting this API version.

  ## Endpoints

  All paths below start with `/api/v1/groups/:groupID/checklist`.

  | Method and suffix | Action | Success data |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `GET` on the base path | Read items and reports | 200, items, summary, member claims and pagination |
  | `POST /items` | Add an item | 201, created item |
  | `PUT /items/:itemID/claim` | Take a group item for yourself | 200, item with its assignee |
  | `DELETE /items/:itemID/claim` | Release your claim | 200, item with a null assignee |
  | `DELETE /items/:itemID` | Delete an item | 200, message |

  ## Item types and filters

  Values are case-sensitive.

  | Field | Values | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `type` | `GROUP`, `PERSONAL` | Claimable group item or shared reminder for everyone to bring their own supplies. |
  | `filter` | `all`, `claimed`, `unclaimed`, `mine`, `personal` | All items, claimed group items, available group items, group items claimed by the caller, or personal reminders. |

  Every item has its own ID. Adding Blanket three times creates three independently claimable rows. An item starts available. Its creator stays the same through claims, releases and member departures.

  ## Access and lifecycle

  All routes require an ACTIVE account, a valid Bearer access token and ACTIVE membership with no departure timestamp. The current group owner controls deletion of claimed items. The server checks permissions on every request.

  | Action | Available group item | Claimed group item | Personal reminder |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | Claim | Any active member, for themselves | Assignee may retry | Unavailable |
  | Release | Already available, safe to retry | Assignee only | Unavailable |
  | Delete | Any active member | Group owner only | Any active member |

  Any active member may add either item type. On concurrent claims by different members, the first succeeds and the other receives `409 CHECKLIST_ITEM_ALREADY_CLAIMED`. Member departure or removal clears that member's surviving claims in the same transaction, including departures the group workflow allows during SETTLING. A later rejoin starts without the former claims. Deletion is soft and removes the item from results and counts.

  SETTLING and CLOSED groups remain readable with `is_frozen: true` and all action flags false. Checklist write routes return `409 CHECKLIST_GROUP_INACTIVE`.

  ## Frontend flow

  1. Initialize the screen with GET and `filter=all`. Use `summary` for the tab badges and progress, and `member_claims` for per-member totals. Both cover the whole checklist on every page and filter.
  2. Split the All tab by `type` and `assigned_to`. Show PERSONAL in the shared reminders section. Use the corresponding GET filter to paginate a section independently.
  3. Compare `assigned_to.member_id` with `viewer_member_id` to display "you". The Show creator toggle controls display of `created_by`. Keep using `assigned_to` for the claim holder.
  4. Use `can_claim`, `can_release` and `can_delete` to enable actions. A checkbox claims an available group item or releases the caller's own claim. Omit it on personal reminders.
  5. Refresh GET for the active filter after a write. If another member claimed the item first, reread the list to show who holds it. If a deletion emptied the last page, request an earlier page.

  Personal reminders contribute to the All and Personal totals. Group progress uses claimed GROUP items divided by all GROUP items. A member's `avatar_url` is optional and temporary. Use an avatar fallback when it is null or expires.

  ## Manual Bruno workflow

  Select Local, set `baseUrl` to the running API and log in through Auth. Set `checklistGroupId`, `checklistItemType` and `checklistItemId` manually. After Create, copy `data.id` to `checklistItemId`. You can also copy an ID from Get. Example IDs are illustrative. Auth Login and Refresh continue to supply the access token.

  1. Create three GROUP items with the same title and one PERSONAL reminder. Verify the IDs and try all five filters in Get Checklist.
  2. Claim a GROUP item as member A. Check that it shows under Mine for A. Use a second active member to compare permissions and exercise competing claims.
  3. As B, try to release or delete an item A holds. Try deleting a separate claimed row as the owner. As A, release your claim and check that it returns to Unclaimed.
  4. Delete a personal reminder with any member and verify that a personal reminder rejects both claim actions. Check that group-only progress stays consistent.
  5. In a test group, have an assignee leave or get removed. Verify the released item and the member counts. Test that SETTLING and CLOSED allow reads and freeze checklist writes.
}
